('ওটেন সাহেবের বাংলো', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/1bb82204a294_136450.jpg', 'শওকত ওসমান', 'সপ্তডিঙা', 'শিশু-কিশোর গল্প', '9789849227328', 'বাংলা', NULL, NULL, 135.0, 119, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'শওকত ওসমানের প্রথম গ্রন্থ ‘ওটেন সাহেবের বাংলাে’ কলকাতায় প্রকাশিত হয় ১৯৪৪ সালে । এটি একটি শিশুতােষ ছােট গল্পের বই। প্রথম প্রকাশেই বেশ নাম করেন। এর মধ্যে ১৯৪৭ সালে দেশভাগ হবার ফলে তিনি কলকাতা থেকে চট্টগ্রামে কমার্স কলেজে বদলি গ্রহণ করেন। জানি না, কি কারণে এই বইটি তিনি দ্বিতীয় সংস্করণ করেননি। এই গল্পের লেখার সঙ্গে আরাে একটি গল্প যােগ করে প্রকাশ করেন ছোটদের নানান গল্প। বর্তমানে আমরা পূর্বরূপটি ফিরিয়ে আনতে চাই। বইটির ঐতিহাসিক মূল্য অনুধাবন করে । আশা করি দেশের শিশু কিশােররা বইটি আগ্রহ নিয়ে সংগ্রহ করবে । Show More'),
('The Laughter of a Slave', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/d439e7bd4_19642.jpg', 'Kabir Chowdhury , Sowkot Osman', 'Adorn Publication', 'Novel: English Language', '9847016900419', 'English', 111, '1st Published, 2008', 150.0, 139, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'The Laughter of a Slave is a moving and powerful tale about the indomitable spirit of man, dramatically personified in the black slave Tatari. The beauty of the slave''s free laughter is expressed through his love for his clandestine wife, the Armenian slave-girl Meherjan. And the poet Abu Ishaq sings of that spirit which chains can fetter but not break. Set in the Caliph Harun-al-Rashid''s exotic Baghdad, full of sensuous scenes of love and cruelty, it is essentially a parable of all times: the glorious struggle of a heroic soul which bends neither to temptation nor to torture, which accepts death but not defeat. The story has a particular relevance in our time, when the noble and defiant spirit of man is subjected to all kinds of pressures by various forces, including the Establishment. The original book in Bengali, entitled Kritadasher Hashi, was awarded the Adamjee Prize for Literature, Pakistan''s Pulitzer Prize. Shawkat Osman ( Sheikh Azizur Rahman; 1917 – 1998) was a Bangladeshi novelist and short story writer.He was born in Sabalsinghapur, Hughli, West Bengal in 1917. His father was Sheikh Mohammad Yehia.He was educated at the Aliah University (Anglo-Persian Department), and at the St. Xavier''s College, Calcutta from where he graduated in 1938. Thereafter, he would earn an MA degree in Bengali literature from the University of Calcutta in 1941. Osman''s first prominent novel was Janani. Janani is a portrait of the disintegration of a family because of the rural and urban divide. In Kritadaser Hasi , Osman explores the darkness of contemporary politics and reality of dictatorship. The Translator : Kabir Chowdhury (1923) is a noted translator, critic and essayist. His elegant and lively English translations of Bengali poems, novels and short stories have been widely acclaimed at home and abroad Show More'),
